+# Stage 9 Validation & Tuning Protocol — `stage9-validation.v1`
+
+Build source: `docs/implementation-order.md` §9 ("Validation & tuning"), the gap review's Top-10
+actions 5 and 10, and ADRs 0004 / 0005 / 0010 plus `docs/specs/historical-episode-schema.md`. This
+document is the **written, reproducible protocol** Stage 9 executes against the Stage 8 gold sets.
+
+It is *only* the protocol and the shared, domain-neutral primitives that support it
+(`services/evaluation/calibration.py`). It selects **no** threshold, changes **no** production
+value, and inspects **no** sealed final holdout. Every domain evaluator named below is a later
+Stage 9 item; this document fixes the rules those items must obey so that when they run, a number
+reported as "held out" actually was.
+
+- **Protocol id / version:** `stage9-validation.v1`
+- **Frozen production thresholds (unchanged by this document):** clustering **0.80** live (roadmap
+  **0.82**); entity linking **accept 0.85 / adjudicate 0.50**; analogy floor **0.60**; alert decision
+  boundary **0.50**. Stage 9 owns any future change to these; `stage9-validation.v1` makes none.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Protocol identity and lifecycle
+
+A run of this protocol on any domain proceeds in three strictly ordered phases with a freeze in the
+middle. Skipping or re-ordering them invalidates the result.
+
+1. **Train — enumerate.** Score every candidate policy on the **train** split. The candidate space
+   is the predeclared grid (§4). Train applies only the *eligibility* gates (hard feasibility
+   filters); it selects nothing.
+2. **Development — select exactly one.** Among the train-eligible candidates, select **exactly one**
+   using the predeclared, deterministic **development objective** (§4). The objective is fixed before
+   any development number is looked at; it is not adjusted to the data.
+3. **Final holdout — report once.** Only after the protocol artifact and the selected parameters are
+   **frozen and hash-verified** (§6) is the **final holdout** scored, exactly once, as a report. The
+   holdout number is never an input to selection.
+
+Freeze discipline:
+
+- Selection and the final report are separated by a freeze. The selected parameters are serialized
+  to a canonical artifact and hashed (`canonical_json_hash`); the protocol document itself is hashed
+  (`sha256_file`) into the frozen manifest.
+- **No retuning after final labels.** If the final holdout result is unsatisfactory, that is a
+  finding, not a do-over. A new attempt requires a **new protocol version** and a **new, unseen
+  holdout** — reusing the same holdout after seeing it converts it into a development set.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Split governance and loaders
+
+| Domain | Gold asset | Split? | Holdout | Stage 9 tuning loader |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Entity linking | `evaluation/gold/entity_linking/v1/` | train 100 / dev 50 / holdout 50 | sealed | `load_tuning_corpus()` (train+dev, holdout excluded by construction) |
+| Alerts | `evaluation/gold/alert_episodes/v1/` | train 24 / dev 12 / holdout 12 | sealed | `load_tuning_corpus()` |
+| Analogy | `db/seed/episodes/analogy_gold.json` | none (40 pairs) | n/a | evaluation-only; `load_corpus_and_gold()` |
+| Clustering | *(none exists)* | n/a | n/a | n/a |
+
+- **Normal tuning code uses `load_tuning_corpus`** (or the individual `load_split("train")` /
+  `load_split("development")` loads). It never calls `load_corpus()` and never passes
+  `allow_holdout=True`. Both entity and alert loaders exclude `final_holdout` from the tuning corpus
+  by construction and refuse `load_split("final_holdout")` without an explicit opt-in.
+- **Entity and alert final holdouts stay sealed** until an explicit, domain-specific **final
+  command** (§6). Only that command's code path may pass the loader's `allow_holdout=True`.
+- **Analogy has no holdout** and is evaluation-only (§4.3): no split, no selection, no tuning.
+- **Clustering has no gold asset** at all (§4.1): its status is `not_verifiable` until one exists.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Determinism and shared primitives
+
+Every Stage 9 artifact must be byte-reproducible from its inputs. The shared, domain-neutral toolkit
+is `services/evaluation/calibration.py`; domain evaluators must build on it and add no source of
+non-determinism.
+
+- **Inclusive Decimal grids.** Candidate grids are generated by `inclusive_decimal_grid(start, stop,
+  step)` using `decimal.Decimal` — both endpoints present, exact multiples of the step, no binary
+  float drift. Bounds are passed as decimal strings/ints, never floats. Ordering is ascending and
+  stable.
+- **Stable ordering.** Cases, candidates, and metric keys are iterated in a fixed order (gold ids are
+  already sorted by the loaders). No iteration depends on set or dict insertion order.
+- **Canonical JSON.** Artifacts are serialized with `canonical_json_bytes` — UTF-8, sorted keys,
+  compact separators, `allow_nan=False`, trailing newline — so a given value has exactly one byte
+  encoding. `canonical_json_hash` is the SHA-256 of those exact bytes; `sha256_file` hashes a file's
+  exact bytes.
+- **Frozen-artifact verification.** `verify_artifact_hash(path, expected_sha256)` recomputes the
+  file's SHA-256 and raises `ArtifactVerificationError` on any mismatch — the check §6 depends on.
+- **No wall-clock, no randomness.** No `datetime.now()`, no seeds, no sampling. Timestamps, if a
+  report needs one, are supplied by the caller and recorded as data, never read from the clock inside
+  the evaluator.
+- **Safe binary metrics.** `BinaryMetrics` is the shared confusion matrix. Its **precision is `None`
+  (undefined) — never 1.0 — when nothing was predicted positive**; every other rate is `None` exactly
+  where its denominator is zero (§4.2, §4.4 restate the domain consequences).
+
+---
+
+## 4. Domain protocols
+
+### 4.1 Clustering (single-link cosine threshold)
+
+- **Do not change either value.** The live default is **0.80** (`cluster_by_similarity`) and the
+  roadmap target is **0.82** (ADR 0004 / §8.4). `stage9-validation.v1` changes neither.
+- **Intended grid:** `inclusive_decimal_grid("0.700", "0.950", "0.005")` — 51 inclusive points.
+- **Pair metrics:** over labeled same-event / different-event article pairs, compute precision,
+  recall, F1, and balanced accuracy (`BinaryMetrics`), where a "predicted positive" is a pair the
+  threshold would place in one cluster.
+- **Selection objective (feasible precision knee):** a threshold is *feasible* when it has **nonzero
+  predicted positives** and **precision ≥ 0.90**; among feasible thresholds, maximize recall, then
+  F1, then proximity to **0.80**, then prefer the higher threshold.
+- **Status: `not_verifiable`.** No clustering gold asset exists. There is no genuine ~100-pair
+  same/different-event dataset (ADR 0004's precondition), so the grid and objective above are the
+  *written* procedure only; they are not run and select nothing until such a dataset exists.
+
+### 4.2 Entity linking (accept / adjudicate bands)
+
+- **Signal weights are fixed.** ADR 0005's stage-2 signal weights are **not** tuned in v1; only the
+  two band thresholds are swept.
+- **Grid:** each of `accept` and `adjudicate` ranges over `inclusive_decimal_grid("0.000", "1.000",
+  "0.005")`, constrained to **`0 ≤ adjudicate < accept ≤ 1`**.
+- **Preserved semantics (unchanged from `services/entities/news_linking.py`):** inclusive band
+  boundaries (`score ≥ accept` accepts, `score ≥ adjudicate` adjudicates), the accept-threshold
+  **tie gate**, the **brand/product gate**, and **4-decimal half-up score rounding** (`round_score`).
+  A candidate policy re-bands the *same* deterministic scores; it never rescores a mention.
+- **Metrics (per policy, computed on scored mentions):** accepted-correct, accepted-wrong-target,
+  accepted-NIL, adjudication count, NIL decisions, candidate recall, top-target recall,
+  auto-accept **precision** and **recall**, routed-link recall (accept **or** adjudicate reaches the
+  correct target), NIL recall, and adjudication rate. **A zero-denominator precision is `None`
+  (infeasible) — never 1.**
+- **Train eligibility:** at least one **automatic accept**, **auto-accept precision ≥ 0.95**, and
+  **NIL recall ≥ 0.80**.
+- **Development selection (lexicographic, first wins):** maximize (1) auto-accept precision, (2)
+  correct auto-link recall, (3) routed-link recall, (4) NIL recall; then minimize (5) adjudication
+  rate, (6) total absolute distance from the initial **0.85 / 0.50**; then prefer (7) higher
+  `accept`, (8) higher `adjudicate`.
+- **Status when run:** `calibrated` if an eligible policy is selected, else
+  `retained_insufficient_evidence` (keep 0.85 / 0.50). **Honest caveat (§7):** the labels are
+  synthetic/automated, English ORG/PRODUCT positives only.
+
+### 4.3 Analogy (retrieval floor)
+
+- **Freeze 0.60.** The minimum-similarity floor stays **0.60** in v1. All 40 gold pairs are
+  unsplit, evaluation-only, and carry **no negative / "no reliable analogy" labels**, so there is no
+  basis on which to *select* a floor.
+- **Metrics (evaluation only):** hit@1 / hit@3 / hit@5, recall@5, MRR, abstention rate, and the
+  threshold diagnostics (correct-above / correct-below / correct-absent) already produced by
+  `services/analogies/evaluation.py`. These describe behavior; they make **no threshold selection and
+  no reranker-quality claim**.
+- **Status: `evaluation_only`.**
+
+### 4.4 Alerts (composite null-model gate)
+
+- **Bands are out of scope.** ADR 0010's severity mapping and raise/clear hysteresis bands are
+  authoritative and are **not** tuned here.
+- **Binary grid (conditional):** `inclusive_decimal_grid("0.10", "0.90", "0.01")` — 81 points — is
+  the intended per-model decision-boundary grid, usable **only when** genuine **outcome-blind**
+  candidate and baseline prediction artifacts exist (per-case predictions produced without seeing the
+  label). They do not exist yet.
+- **Per-model selection on train (each model independently):** require at least one alert and at
+  least one **true positive**; then maximize precision, mean true-positive **lead time**, recall,
+  proximity to **0.50**, then prefer the higher threshold.
+- **Fixed-threshold evaluation:** the selected fixed threshold is evaluated **per required window**
+  (2007-2009, 2020, 2023 — `REQUIRED_WINDOWS`) on development and, after freeze, on final.
+- **Gate-aggregation zeros (distinct from §3's undefined-precision rule):** for the **release
+  gate**, a window with **no alerts** scores precision **0**, and mean lead time with **no true
+  positives** scores **0** — the fail-closed convention of
+  `services/alerts/experimental.py`'s `WindowEvidence`. (The §4.2/§3 `precision = None` rule governs
+  *candidate selection*, where predicting nothing is infeasible; the gate instead treats a
+  no-evidence window as a failing 0. The two never share a call site.)
+- **Release rule:** the candidate must **strictly beat** the baseline
+  (`services/crisis_model/baseline.py`) on **both** precision **and** mean true-positive lead time in
+  **every** required window. A tie, a missing window, or a window with no labels **fails**.
+- **Status: `not_verifiable`.** Current onset indicators cannot be invented into
+  `CountrySignalPanel` values, and the one-shot-per-window cases cannot demonstrate temporal
+  lead-time superiority. The `ExperimentalGate` evidence stays **empty**, so every composite alert
+  remains experimental and the **single-signal carve-out** remains released.
+
+---
+
+## 5. Report schema and status vocabulary
+
+Every domain run emits one canonical report (serialized with `canonical_json_bytes`) carrying at
+least:
+
+- **protocol** id (`stage9-validation.v1`) and the protocol document's SHA-256 hash;
+- **input hashes** — the exact bytes of every gold split / artifact consumed;
+- **domain** and **status** (below);
+- **split** evaluated (train / development / final);
+- **model / policy versions** (embedding model+version, linker weight-set id, baseline id, etc.);
+- the **evaluated grid** (bounds + step, or "n/a");
+- the **selected parameters** — or the explicit statement that the production value is **unchanged**;
+- the **metrics** (§4);
+- **limitations / blockers** (§7).
+
+**Status vocabulary** (`CalibrationStatus`, validated by `validate_status`):
+
+| Status | Meaning |
+|---|---|
+| `calibrated` | A parameter was selected on development against the predeclared objective. |
+| `retained_insufficient_evidence` | The gold set exists but the eligibility gate was not met; the production value is kept. |
+| `evaluation_only` | Measured and reported only; no threshold is selected (analogy). |
+| `not_verifiable` | The evidence needed to verify anything does not yet exist (clustering; alerts today). |
+
+Under `stage9-validation.v1` today: clustering `not_verifiable`, entity linking (when run)
+`calibrated` or `retained_insufficient_evidence`, analogy `evaluation_only`, alerts `not_verifiable`.
+
+---
+
+## 6. Final-holdout unseal preconditions
+
+The domain-specific **final command** is the only code path permitted to pass the loader's
+`allow_holdout=True`. It must refuse to run unless **all** of the following hold:
+
+1. the **protocol artifact hash matches** the frozen manifest (`verify_artifact_hash`);
+2. the **selected parameters exist and are immutable** — serialized, hashed, and unmodified since the
+   development selection;
+3. the **development report exists** (selection happened before the holdout is touched);
+4. the domain's **input and model artifacts are complete** (all gold splits present and valid, model
+   version pinned);
+5. the **output path does not already exist** (a one-time report is never silently overwritten);
+6. an **explicit acknowledgement flag** is set by the operator for this one run.
+
+If any precondition fails, the final command aborts without opening the holdout. A failed final
+result does not license retuning — it requires a new protocol version and a new, unseen holdout (§1).
+
+---
+
+## 7. Honest limitations
+
+These are recorded on every report; none is a defect to hide.
+
+- **Entity linking:** labels are **synthetic / automated**, English **ORG/PRODUCT** positives only;
+  no human adjudication and no coreference. Any `calibrated` result is a calibration against
+  *automated* labels, not a human-validated ground truth.
+- **Alerts:** labels are automated and there are **no mapped model inputs** — the onset indicators do
+  not map to live `CountrySignalPanel` values, and each window holds too few, one-shot cases to prove
+  temporal lead-time superiority. Hence `not_verifiable` and an empty `ExperimentalGate`.
+- **Analogy:** **zero human sign-offs**, **no negative / no-reliable-analogy labels**, and **no
+  split** — strictly evaluation-only, never a selection basis.
+- **Clustering:** **no labeled same/different-event pairs exist**, so the procedure in §4.1 is
+  written but not run; status stays `not_verifiable` until a genuine ~100-pair dataset is curated.
